# A trailing line comment that does not fit even once the code before it breaks leaves the code as it is and
# is wrapped in its own column. A second run reads the wrapped part as part of the comment and leaves it there.
----------
class T {
  public static void main(String[] args) { // one long incredibly unbroken sentence moving from topic to topic so that no-one had a chance to interrupt;
  }
}
----------
class T {
    public static void main(String[] args) { // one long incredibly unbroken sentence moving from topic to topic so that
                                             // no-one had a chance to interrupt;
    }
}
